    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d560">

                <pb facs="1081" n="1037" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v05p1/pg1037"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.5/8–2054</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Prime Minister Churchill to the Secretary of
                            State
                    </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d560-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1954-08-14">August 14,
                        1954</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Foster</hi>:]</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>I have strongly supported your line in my messages to Mendes-France. I have indeed for
                        a very long time, as you know, been wearied with this deeply injurious
                        French procedure of delay. I hope however you will not fail to grip the
                            NATO solution which I am sure can be
                        arranged.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>I am telegraphing to you because in Anthony’s absence
                        on holiday I have been promoted to the Foreign Office. I hope therefore you
                        will treat me as kindly as you did when we talked about my Boston speech. I
                        suppose you are watching the Attlee and Bevan
                        excursion. How lucky you are in Washington never to have to worry about
                        party politics.</item>
                </list>
                <p>Kindest regards,</p>
                <closer>[<signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winston Churchill</hi>
                        
                    </signed>]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d560-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d560-f1-content">
                <p>Source text was transmitted to the Embassy in the United Kingdom in telegram 1030
                    to London, Aug. 20, together with the texts of a similar message dated Aug. 19
                        (<ref target="#pg1050">p. 1050</ref>) and a message from Dulles to Churchill dated Aug. 20 (<ref
                        target="#pg1051">p. 1051</ref>).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
